@support_reactionary
subtitle: This is the default option.
on-arrival: progressive_dissent += 10 if braun_campaign; dvp_candidate = reactionary_candidate

We will support [+ reactionary_candidate +] in this election.

- @endorsements_reactionary: Scout out potential endorsements.

@endorsements_reactionary
view-if: braun_campaign

We can try to convince parties supporting other candidates to switch their support to [+ reactionary_candidate +].

- @convince_z_reactionary: Convince the Center Party to back [+ reactionary_candidate +].
- @convince_ddp_reactionary: Convince the [+ ddp_name +] to back [+ reactionary_candidate +].
- @convince_dbp_reactionary: Convince the DBP to back [+ reactionary_candidate +].
- @convince_spd_reactionary: Convince the SPD to back [+ reactionary_candidate +].
- @convince_csrp_reactionary: Convince the CSRP to back [+ reactionary_candidate +].
- @view_candidates: View party endorsements.
- @hope: We have concluded negotiations with other parties.

@convince_z_reactionary
view-if: z_candidate != reactionary_candidate
go-to: convince_z_success_reactionary if z_relation >= 40; convince_z_fail_reactionary if z_relation < 40
max-visits: 1

We try to convince the Center Party to support [+ reactionary_candidate +].

@convince_z_success_reactionary
on-arrival: z_relation += 3; z_candidate = reactionary_candidate; braun_votes -= (z_normalized - bvp_votes) if z_candidate = "Braun"
go-to: endorsements_reactionary

Thanks to our friendly relations and connections with their right wing, the Center Party is now campaigning for [+reactionary_candidate+] in the election.

@convince_z_fail_reactionary
on-arrival: z_relation -= 3
go-to: endorsements_reactionary

Unfortunately, the Center Party has refused to support [+ reactionary_candidate +] for the presidency.


@convince_dbp_reactionary
view-if: dbp_exist and dbp_candidate != reactionary_candidate
go-to: convince_dbp_success_reactionary if dbp_relation >= 40; convince_dbp_fail_reactionary if dbp_relation < 40
max-visits: 1

We try to convince the DBP to support [+ reactionary_candidate +].

@convince_dbp_success_reactionary
on-arrival: dbp_relation += 3; dbp_candidate = reactionary_candidate; braun_votes -= dbp_normalized if dbp_candidate = "Braun"
go-to: endorsements_reactionary

Thanks to our friendly relations, the DBP is now campaigning for [+ reactionary_candidate +] in the election.

@convince_dbp_fail_reactionary
on-arrival: dbp_relation -= 3
go-to: endorsements_reactionary

Unfortunately, the DBP has refused to support [+ reactionary_candidate +] for the presidency.


@convince_csrp_reactionary
view-if: csrp_exist and csrp_candidate != reactionary_candidate
go-to: convince_csrp_success_reactionary if csrp_relation >= 45; convince_csrp_fail_reactionary if csrp_relation < 45
max-visits: 1

We try to convince the CSRP to support [+ reactionary_candidate +].

@convince_csrp_success_reactionary
on-arrival: csrp_relation += 3; csrp_candidate = reactionary_candidate; braun_votes -= csrp_normalized if csrp_candidate = "Braun"
go-to: endorsements_reactionary

Thanks to our friendly relations, the CSRP is now campaigning for [+ reactionary_candidate +] in the election.

@convince_csrp_fail_reactionary
on-arrival: csrp_relation -= 3
go-to: endorsements_reactionary

Unfortunately, the CSRP has refused to support [+ reactionary_candidate +] for the presidency.

@convince_ddp_reactionary
view-if: ddp_exist and ddp_candidate != reactionary_candidate
go-to: convince_ddp_success_reactionary if ddp_relation >= 40; convince_ddp_fail_reactionary if ddp_relation < 40
max-visits: 1

The liberal vote has been falling over time, especially during the current economic depression, so they will probably be of minimal help to us. Still, every little bit counts.

@convince_ddp_success_reactionary
on-arrival: ddp_relation += 5; ddp_candidate = reactionary_candidate; braun_votes -= ddp_normalized if ddp_candidate = "Braun"
go-to: endorsements_reactionary

Thanks to our friendly relations and connections with their business wing, the [+ ddp_name +] is now campaigning for [+ reactionary_candidate +] in the election.

@convince_ddp_fail_reactionary
on-arrival: ddp_relation -= 5
go-to: endorsements_reactionary

Unfortunately, under the influence of their left wing, the [+ ddp_name +] has refused to support [+ reactionary_candidate +] for the presidency. 


@convince_spd_reactionary
choose-if: braun_votes < (hitler_votes + harzburg_votes)
unavailable-subtitle: The Social Democrats are stronger than the far-right.
go-to: convince_spd_success_reactionary if (dvp_left >= 0 and spd_relation >= 50); convince_spd_fail_reactionary if (dvp_left < 0 or spd_relation < 50)
max-visits: 1

We remind the SPD leaders that, despite his known reactionary nature, [+ reactionary_candidate +] has at least been keeping the Nazis at bay.

@convince_spd_success_reactionary
on-arrival: spd_relation += 3; spd_candidate = reactionary_candidate; braun_campaign = 0 if braun_campaign; ddp_candidate = reactionary_candidate if ddp_candidate = "Braun"; dbp_candidate = reactionary_candidate if dbp_candidate = "Braun"; csrp_candidate = reactionary_candidate if csrp_candidate = "Braun"; z_candidate = reactionary_candidate if z_candidate = "Braun"
go-to: endorsements_reactionary

The SPD is convinced! They will be part of the [+ reactionary_candidate +] coalition.

@convince_spd_fail_reactionary
on-arrival: spd_relation -= 3
go-to: endorsements_reactionary

Unfortunately, we fail to turn the SPD away from [+ spd_candidate+]. 



@run_eckener
choose-if: dvp_left >= 0
view-if: reactionary_candidate != "Hindenburg"
unavailable-subtitle: Why would we run a republican candidate?
subtitle: After nominating him, we still have to convince the other parties to support him.
on-departure: nationalist_dissent += 10; eckener_campaign = 1; dvp_candidate = "Eckener"; ddp_candidate = "Eckener" if ddp_candidate = reactionary_candidate; spd_candidate = "Eckener" if spd_candidate = reactionary_candidate

We will run Hugo Eckener.

The [? if ddp_candidate = reactionary_candidate: [+ ddp_name +] ?][? if spd_candidate = reactionary_candidate and ddp_candidate = reactionary_candidate: and ?][? if spd_candidate = reactionary_candidate: SPD ?] will support our candidate, instead of [+ reactionary_candidate +].

- @endorsements_dvp_candidate: Scout out potential endorsements.

@run_jarres
choose-if: dvp_left < 0 and resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: [? if dvp_left >= 0: The party prefers running Luther. ?][? if resources < 2: Not enough resources. ?]
subtitle: After nominating him, we still have to convince the other parties to support him.
on-departure: nationalist_dissent += 10; eckener_campaign = 1; dvp_candidate = "Jarres"; wp_candidate = "Jarres" if wp_candidate = reactionary_candidate

We will run Karl Jarres.

- @endorsements_dvp_candidate: Scout out potential endorsements.

@run_luther
choose-if: dvp_left >= 0 and resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: [? if dvp_left < 0: The party prefers running Jarres. ?][? if resources < 2: Not enough resources. ?]
subtitle: After nominating him, we still have to convince the other parties to support him.
on-departure: nationalist_dissent += 10; eckener_campaign = 1; dvp_candidate = "Luther"; ddp_candidate = "Luther" if ddp_candidate = reactionary_candidate; spd_candidate = "Luther" if spd_candidate = reactionary_candidate

We will run Hans Luther.

The [? if ddp_candidate = reactionary_candidate: [+ ddp_name +] ?][? if spd_candidate = reactionary_candidate and ddp_candidate = reactionary_candidate: and ?][? if spd_candidate = reactionary_candidate: SPD ?] will support our candidate, instead of [+ reactionary_candidate +].

- @endorsements_dvp_candidate: Scout out potential endorsements.

@endorsements_dvp_candidate
view-if: (spd_candidate != dvp_candidate) or (ddp_candidate != dvp_candidate and ddp_exist) or (dbp_candidate != dvp_candidate and dbp_exist) or (z_candidate != dvp_candidate) or (csvd_candidate != dvp_candidate and csvd_exist) or (wp_candidate != dvp_candidate and wp_exist) or (kvp_candidate != dvp_candidate and kvp_formed)

We can try to convince parties supporting other candidates to switch their support to [+ dvp_candidate +].

